+1. **S-1 (High), pay posted for two or more countries keeps one country's line and drops the rest** (persona-beta-2-45-54). Under a Location filter the site then says the pay isn't posted for a place the posting does give pay for.
+   - google:111420466312159942, "Customer Engineer, Migrations Specialist" (Milan · Hamburg · London), posts "Germany: €150000 - €153000 (EUR)" and "Italy: €124000 - €127000 (EUR)". With #c=google&l=Milan, the card says "Pay posted for Germany only (€150K–153K is the pay posted for Germany, not for Milan)" and the drawer "Posted for Germany, not Milan".
+   - google:123907061523063494, "Associate Product Marketing Manager BS/MS Intern", posts Ireland €47000, Germany €53000 and France €41500. Only €47,000 is served. Paris says "Pay posted for Ireland only". The drawer shows both "Several pay ranges" ("this figure is one of them") and "One number, not a range", and neither of the other two figures appears anywhere.
+   - google:111289074672640710, "Program Manager, 3PL", posts Ireland €116–118K and Netherlands €124–127K. Dublin says "Pay posted for the Netherlands only".
+   - Scope per the reviewer: 13 of 13 Google postings with "<Country>: €X (EUR)" lines for 2+ countries, a lower bound from a regex over dist/beta/api/desc/google. Each is served with salary.ranges empty and one country's figure, and the CSV's salary_ranges is empty for them too.
+   - Cause (the reviewer's reading; confirm it): server/salary.js, DQ-15's line selection (~l.394; unitCountry ~l.952). The per-country lines are scored and one is picked; the others are never stored.
+   - Fix: keep every country line as a range with its country, as the degree lines became levels (SA-4), so payAt can price each place. The headline stays the line DQ-15 picks for the posting's main country, and the card, the drawer's "Pay by place", the CSV and Juice use each country's own line.
+   - Find every posting of the 2026-10-16 crawl with pay lines for more than one country or place, on all seven boards and the main site (USD lines by US state or zone too, not only euro countries), and say how many had rows dropped before. Show before and after counts per board, and prove no posting or row was dropped: every posted line is stored.
+   - Bump NORMALIZER_VERSION to norm-14 if the output changes. fix-data-6, running beside you, also bumps to norm-14 for its gazetteer change. Use the same 'norm-14', and re-baseline the golden file and the refresh fixtures with the tooling for your change only (`UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 GOLDEN_REASON=...`, make-fixtures.mjs), never by hand. The lead re-baselines once more after integrating both. Say how many hashes changed and why.
